WEBVTT

00:00:00.598 --> 00:00:02.902
LAST_VALUE often surprises students.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:07.942
The function does not automatically look to the final row of the partition.

00:00:07.942 --> 00:00:11.722
It returns the last value in the current frame.

00:00:11.722 --> 00:00:16.402
With the default ordered frame, that frame commonly ends at the current peer group.

00:00:16.402 --> 00:00:22.442
If you want the final value across the entire partition, make the frame extend through unbounded following.

00:00:22.442 --> 00:00:26.962
Running and moving calculations depend on the window frame.

00:00:26.962 --> 00:00:33.432
Defaults can be surprising, especially with duplicate ordering values or LAST_VALUE.

00:00:33.432 --> 00:00:36.857
Write the frame explicitly when the intended range matters.

00:00:36.857 --> 00:00:41.826
A clear frame makes the query easier to audit and protects against subtle changes in data.
